<section class="wrap section">
  <h1 class="sec-title">Provably Fair</h1>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-h"><h2>Verify a draw</h2></div>
    <p class="muted">Every draw commits to its secret seed before it closes by publishing the seed's SHA-256 hash. After the draw the seed is revealed, so anyone can recompute the hash and the winning number.</p>
    <form action="/fairness" method="GET" class="filters">
      <div class="field inline">
        <label for="draw_id">Draw ID</label>
        <input type="text" id="draw_id" name="draw_id" value="<%= (typeof result !== 'undefined' && result && result.draw) ? result.draw.id : '' %>" placeholder="e.g. 123">
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-p">Verify</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <% if (typeof result !== 'undefined' && result && result.notFound) { %>
  <div class="card mt"><p class="flash f-err">Draw not found. Check the draw ID and try again.</p></div>
  <% } %>

  <% if (typeof result !== 'undefined' && result && result.draw) { %>
  <div class="card mt">
    <div class="card-h"><h2>Verification result &mdash; draw #<%= result.draw.id %></h2></div>
    <div class="slip-lines">
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Draw</span><span><%= result.draw.draw_type %> &middot; <%= result.draw.draw_date %><% if (result.draw.is_test) { %> <span class="badge b-warn">TEST</span><% } %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Published seed hash</span><span class="code"><%= result.draw.seed_hash %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Recomputed hash of revealed seed</span><span class="code"><%= result.recomputed_hash || '—' %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Hash match</span><span><%- (result.hash_match === null || result.hash_match === undefined) ? (result.state === 'cancelled' ? '<span class="badge b-err">Cancelled</span>' : '<span class="badge b-warn">Not settled yet</span>') : (result.hash_match ? '<span class="badge b-ok">&#10003; MATCH</span>' : '<span class="badge b-err">&#10007; MISMATCH</span>') %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Revealed seed</span><span class="code"><%= result.draw.seed || '—' %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Published winning number</span><span><%= (result.draw.winning_number === null || result.draw.winning_number === undefined) ? '—' : result.draw.winning_number %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Recomputed winning number</span><span><%= (result.recomputed_number === null || result.recomputed_number === undefined) ? '—' : result.recomputed_number %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Number match</span><span><%- result.number_note === 'test_override' ? '<span class="badge b-warn">TEST draw — operator-set number</span>' : ((result.number_match === null || result.number_match === undefined) ? (result.state === 'cancelled' ? '<span class="badge b-err">Cancelled — stakes refunded</span>' : '<span class="badge b-warn">Not settled yet</span>') : (result.number_match ? '<span class="badge b-ok">&#10003; MATCH</span>' : '<span class="badge b-err">&#10007; MISMATCH</span>')) %></span></div>
      <% if (result.number_note === 'test_override') { %><p class="muted">This TEST draw's winning number was set for testing, so there is no derived number to recompute. The seed hash above still verifies the draw's committed seed.</p><% } %>
      <% if (result.draw.beacon_status) { %>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Beacon</span><span>drand round <%= result.draw.beacon_round %> — <%= result.draw.beacon_status %></span></div>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Beacon randomness</span><span class="code"><%= result.draw.beacon_randomness || '—' %></span></div>
      <% } else { %>
      <div class="slip-line"><span>Beacon</span><span class="muted">Earlier draw — no beacon was recorded for this draw.</span></div>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="card mt">
    <div class="card-h"><h2>How provably-fair works</h2></div>
    <ol class="fair-steps">
      <li><strong>Commit.</strong> Before the draw closes, the operator generates a secret random seed and publishes its SHA-256 hash (<span class="code">seed_hash</span>). The hash is a one-way fingerprint: it cannot be reversed to reveal the seed.</li>
      <li><strong>Draw.</strong> Once betting closes, the winning number is derived from the seed combined with the public drand beacon randomness for that round, using rejection sampling (no modulo bias): <span class="code">winning_number = reject_sample(SHA256(seed + '|' + beacon_randomness), draw_id)</span>. Because the hash was published first and the beacon is public and unpredictable, the operator cannot change the outcome afterwards. Earlier draws with no beacon recorded used the legacy <span class="code">(HMAC(seed) mod 15) + 1</span> derivation.</li>
      <li><strong>Reveal &amp; verify.</strong> The seed is revealed. Anyone can compute <span class="code">SHA256(seed)</span> and compare it with the published hash, then recompute the winning number from the seed. If both match, the draw was fair.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
